PROTOCOL_VERSION 0.1.0

NAME Upstream Contribution Protocol

STATUS APPROVED

OWNER President Cley Duarte

DATE 2026-07-28

SCOPE PACE

ORIGIN REQUEST-0006 (PACE independence and upstream), enforced by RULE-0006.

PURPOSE

Define exactly how an improvement that is DISCOVERED inside a consumer
project reaches PACE the engine - and how it does not. PACE is independent;
consumer projects (e.g. TuPerimetro) are adopters, never dependencies. An
improvement becomes part of PACE only with the ROOT_AUTHORITY's explicit
authorization. Nothing flows upstream silently.

PRINCIPLE

The boundary between a consumer's .pace/ and the PACE engine is
deliberate. A consumer never waits for PACE to keep working, and PACE
never absorbs a change just because a consumer made it. Improvements are
optional gifts, authorized one at a time.

FLOW

1  DISCOVERY
   While using PACE, a consumer project (or its AI) finds something worth
   upstreaming: a better .pace/ structure, a new engine capability, a rule,
   a standard, a protocol. It stays in the consumer until proposed.

2  PROPOSAL
   The improvement is logged as a REQUEST in PACE's own intake
   (.pace/requests/, SCOPE PACE), recording WHO, DATE, RAW_TEXT and the
   ORIGIN consumer project. Proposing is not adopting.

3  REVIEW
   The AI ADVISES and AUDITS; it never decides (RULE-0003). It may argue for
   or against, surface risks, and show how the change would look.

4  AUTHORIZATION
   Only on the ROOT_AUTHORITY's explicit approval does the REQUEST get
   PROMOTED_TO an official artifact - a rule (pace rule add), a standard, a
   protocol, or an engine change on a roadmap item. Approval is the gate.

5  ATTRIBUTION
   The origin project is credited in the promoted artifact (PROMOTED_FROM /
   ORIGIN). Credit does not create dependency: PACE still stands alone.

6  NO SILENT UPSTREAM
   No change moves from a consumer into PACE automatically, in bulk, or by
   default. Every upstream step is an explicit, authorized decision - and,
   once approved, is captured in .pace/ in the same turn (RULE-0008).

CONSUMER_SIDE

The consumer keeps and evolves its own .pace/ freely. Upstreaming is
optional and never blocks the consumer. Downstream, the consumer adopts
new PACE engine versions on its own schedule (pip install --upgrade),
with no forced migration - old instances stay valid.

END
